.TH "MCP-SERVER-AHA-AQL" "1" "November 2026" "mcp-server-aha-aql 0.24.0" "User Commands"
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
mcp-server-aha-aql - MCP server for Aha!
with the query language AQL
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]mcp-server-aha-aql stdio\f[R] [subdomain=\f[I]NAME\f[R]]
[api-key-file=\f[I]PATH\f[R]] [default-product=\f[I]PRODUCT\f[R]]
[read-only=true]
.PP
\f[B]mcp-server-aha-aql http\f[R] [listen=\f[I]HOST:PORT\f[R]]
[subdomain=\f[I]NAME\f[R]] [default-product=\f[I]PRODUCT\f[R]]
[read-only=true]
.PP
\f[B]mcp-server-aha-aql query\f[R] query=\f[I]STATEMENT\f[R]
[subdomain=\f[I]NAME\f[R]] [api-key-file=\f[I]PATH\f[R]]
[default-product=\f[I]PRODUCT\f[R]] [read-only=true]
.PP
\f[B]mcp-server-aha-aql execute\f[R] statement=\f[I]STATEMENT\f[R]
[dry-run=true] [subdomain=\f[I]NAME\f[R]] [api-key-file=\f[I]PATH\f[R]]
[default-product=\f[I]PRODUCT\f[R]] [read-only=true]
.PP
\f[B]mcp-server-aha-aql \[en]version\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\f[B]mcp-server-aha-aql\f[R] is an MCP (Model Context Protocol) server
for the Aha!
product management service.
A language model reads and changes Aha!
records through one query language, AQL, and two tools.
The tool \f[B]query\f[R] reads records.
The tool \f[B]execute\f[R] creates, changes or deletes one record.
.PP
The server calls the Aha!
REST API at https://\f[I]subdomain\f[R].aha.io/api/v1.
It sends requests to no other host.
The only other host that it connects to is the HTTPS proxy of the
environment.
.SH MODES
.PP
The first word of the command line selects the mode.
.TP
\f[B]stdio\f[R]
MCP over standard input and standard output.
The process works with one Aha!
account.
.TP
\f[B]http\f[R]
MCP over HTTP on the endpoint /mcp.
Every request brings its credential in the header \f[B]Aha-Api-Key\f[R],
and its account name in the header \f[B]Aha-Subdomain\f[R] when the
server has no setting subdomain.
A request with an \f[B]Origin\f[R] header is refused with status 403.
The server keeps no MCP session: no answer has the header
\f[B]Mcp-Session-Id\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]query\f[R]
Command word.
One call of the tool query, then the program ends.
Selects no transport.
.TP
\f[B]execute\f[R]
Command word.
One call of the tool execute, then the program ends.
Selects no transport.
.PP
Another first word gives the message \[lq]error: unknown transport
`\f[I]word\f[R]'.
Valid: stdio, http, query, execute\[rq] and the exit code 2.
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
All options have the form \f[I]key\f[R]=\f[I]value\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]subdomain\f[R]=\f[I]NAME\f[R]
The account name: the part of the address before .aha.io.
Variable: \f[B]AHA_SUBDOMAIN\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]api-key-file\f[R]=\f[I]PATH\f[R]
The path of a file that has the credential.
Only the owner may read the file.
Not in http mode.
.TP
\f[B]default-product\f[R]=\f[I]PRODUCT\f[R]
The key, the numeric id or the name of a product.
Tool descriptions and examples use its key.
Variable: \f[B]AHA_DEFAULT_PRODUCT\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]read-only\f[R]=true|false
With true the tool execute is not offered.
Variable: \f[B]AHA_READ_ONLY\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]listen\f[R]=\f[I]HOST:PORT\f[R]
The listen address in http mode.
Default: 127.0.0.1:8080.
A warning is written when the host is not a loopback address.
.TP
\f[B]dry-run\f[R]=true|false
Word execute only.
The statement is checked completely, and no write request is sent.
.TP
\f[B]query\f[R]=\f[I]STATEMENT\f[R]
The statement for the word query.
With \f[B]-\f[R] the statement is read from standard input.
.TP
\f[B]statement\f[R]=\f[I]STATEMENT\f[R]
The statement for the word execute.
With \f[B]-\f[R] the statement is read from standard input.
.TP
\f[B]\[en]version\f[R]
Writes the version and the SHA256 of the specification, then ends.
.PP
An option takes precedence over its environment variable.
No option takes the credential itself.
.SH TOOLS
.TP
\f[B]query\f[R]
One parameter, \f[I]query\f[R]: one AQL statement.
SELECT fields FROM entity [WHERE field = `value' [AND \&...]] [GROUP BY
field] [ORDER BY field [DESC]] [LIMIT n], or DESCRIBE entity.
Entities: products, releases, features, epics, requirements,
initiatives, goals, ideas, comments, users, statuses, me.
Custom fields are written custom.key.
.TP
\f[B]execute\f[R]
One parameter, \f[I]statement\f[R]: one AQL statement.
INSERT INTO entity (parent, field, \&...)
VALUES (`parent id', `value', \&...), UPDATE entity SET field = `value',
\&...
WHERE id = `id', or DELETE FROM entity WHERE id = `id'.
In stdio and http mode each call writes one log line to standard error.
.PP
The answers to \f[I]initialize\f[R] and \f[I]server/discover\f[R] have
server instructions.
The one MCP prompt, \f[B]start\f[R] (\[lq]How to start with AQL\[rq]),
has no argument and gives a short guide to the first statements.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\f[B]AHA_SUBDOMAIN\f[R]
The setting subdomain.
.TP
\f[B]AHA_API_KEY\f[R]
The credential in stdio mode and manual mode, when the option
api-key-file is absent.
Not read in http mode.
.TP
\f[B]AHA_DEFAULT_PRODUCT\f[R]
The setting default_product.
.TP
\f[B]AHA_READ_ONLY\f[R]
The setting read_only: true or false.
.TP
\f[B]HTTPS_PROXY\f[R], \f[B]https_proxy\f[R], \f[B]NO_PROXY\f[R], \f[B]no_proxy\f[R]
The proxy for the connection to Aha!.
The Go standard library reads them.
.TP
\f[B]SSL_CERT_FILE\f[R], \f[B]SSL_CERT_DIR\f[R]
The trust store on Linux.
The Go standard library reads them.
On macOS the trust store is the keychain, and on Windows it is the
certificate store of the system; the two variables have no effect there.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
\f[B]0\f[R]
Manual mode: the tool returned a result.
stdio and http: the server ended normally, after end of input, SIGTERM
or SIGINT.
.TP
\f[B]1\f[R]
Manual mode: the statement failed; the message is on standard error.
http: the listen address cannot be bound.
.TP
\f[B]2\f[R]
The command line or the configuration is wrong.
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
mcp-server-aha-aql query query=\[dq]SELECT id, name, status FROM features WHERE release = \[aq]DEMO-R-3\[aq]\[dq]
mcp-server-aha-aql execute dry-run=true statement=\[dq]UPDATE features SET status = \[aq]Shipped\[aq] WHERE id = \[aq]DEMO-23\[aq]\[dq]
mcp-server-aha-aql http listen=127.0.0.1:8080 subdomain=mycompany
\f[R]
.fi
